<title>MEXICO: Bufete to get $40 mln for Argentina sale.</title>
<headline>Bufete to get $40 mln for Argentina sale.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction and engineering company Bufete Industrial said on Tuesday it would obtain $40 million from the sale of Mexpetrol's 67 percent stake in Mexpetrol Argentina, a company news release said.</p>
<p>Bufete said it had received $35.4 million of the total as of May 12 and would receive the remainder shortly. The company said it would use the proceeds mainly to retire debt.</p>
<p>Mexpetrol sold its share in Mexpetrol Argentina to Argentine companies Yacimientos Petroliferos Fiscales and Astra.</p>
<p>Mexpetrol is a joint venture between Mexican state-owned oil corporation Petroleos Mexicanos and private Mexican companies, including Bufete and fellow construction company ICA SA.</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907))</p>
